      "writtenOn": "2018-02-17T03:28:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are mixing up looping over only valid entries with counting the number of entries. You should continue using the cpufreq_for_each_entry() as you did before even if you use cpufreq_frequency_table_get_index() later on. Take a look at those macros and you\u0027ll see what I mean.\n\nAs you have written the code, you\u0027ll definitely be overflowing the allocated memory in acct_update and record_transition functions.\n\nAnd your stats will also be wrong if there are invalid freqs",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "25866078274b014a87e4b03f112d6ee0329a4414",
